  data: {
    LLM: "All players look around at each other. The Candyman secretly winks at Buyers to make deals. When a Buyer is winked at, they reveal their card, say 'Sold!' (or 'The deal has been made!'), and retire from the round. They must NOT reveal who the Candyman is. The Cop watches for who is winking. When the Cop thinks they know who the Candyman is, they say 'busted' and point at the accused. The accused reveals their card. If correct (Ace), round ends. If wrong (Buyer), round continues - but now everyone knows who the Cop is. Alternative signals: If winking is difficult, players can agree on another signal like tapping the face.",
    Player: "All players look around at each other. The Candyman secretly winks at Buyers to make deals. When a Buyer is winked at, they reveal their card, say 'Sold!' (or 'The deal has been made!'), and retire from the round. They must NOT reveal who the Candyman is. The Cop watches for who is winking. When the Cop thinks they know who the Candyman is, they say 'busted' and point at the accused. The accused reveals their card. If correct (Ace), round ends. If wrong (Buyer), round continues - but now everyone knows who the Cop is. Alternative signals: If winking is difficult, players can agree on another signal like tapping the face.",
    objective: 'Candyman: Sell candy to as many Buyers as possible without being caught. Buyers: Successfully buy candy by receiving a wink from the Candyman. Cop: Identify and expose the Candyman before all Buyers complete their purchases.',
    gameplay: "All players look around at each other. The Candyman secretly winks at Buyers to make deals. When a Buyer is winked at, they reveal their card, say 'Sold!' (or 'The deal has been made!'), and retire from the round. They must NOT reveal who the Candyman is. The Cop watches for who is winking. When the Cop thinks they know who the Candyman is, they say 'busted' and point at the accused. The accused reveals their card. If correct (Ace), round ends. If wrong (Buyer), round continues - but now everyone knows who the Cop is. Alternative signals: If winking is difficult, players can agree on another signal like tapping the face.",
    keyRules: [
      'Only the Candyman can wink (or use agreed signal)',
      'Buyers who complete a deal reveal their card and retire',
      'Buyers must NOT reveal who the Candyman is',
      'Cop can make multiple accusations but loses points for wrong ones',
      'After first wrong accusation, everyone knows who the Cop is',
      'Round ends when Candyman is busted OR all Buyers have bought',
    ],
