    turnFlow: "All players look around at each other. The Candyman secretly winks at Buyers to make deals. When a Buyer is winked at, they reveal their card, say 'Sold!' (or 'The deal has been made!'), and retire from the round. They must NOT reveal who the Candyman is. The Cop watches for who is winking. When the Cop thinks they know who the Candyman is, they say 'busted' and point at the accused. The accused reveals their card. If correct (Ace), round ends. If wrong (Buyer), round continues - but now everyone knows who the Cop is. Alternative signals: If winking is difficult, players can agree on another signal like tapping the face.",
